   "he": "רַבִּי יוֹסֵי אוֹמֵר כּוּ׳. מַאי ״עוֹקֶץ״? אָמַר שְׁמוּאֵל: עוּקְצוֹ שֶׁל דַּד.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches that «Rabbi Yosei says:» Grown womanhood begins when the breasts have developed to a size where if a person places his hand on the nipple [oketz] it depresses and slows to return. The Gemara asks: «What» is the meaning of «oketz? Shmuel said:» It means «the protrusion [oketz] of the breast,» i.e., the nipple."
